</header><div class="entry-content">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This tutorial will walk you through reading public and limited-access information on an ORCID record using the public or member API. It is based on version 3.0 of the ORCID message schema.  </p>


<div role="navigation" aria-label="Table of Contents" class="simpletoc wp-block-simpletoc-toc"><ol class="simpletoc-list">
<li><a href="#h-get-some-client-credentials">Get some client credentials</a>
</li>
<li><a href="#h-get-an-access-token">Get an access token</a>
</li>
<li><a href="#h-decide-what-you-want-to-read">Decide what you want to read</a>
</li>
<li><a href="#h-use-the-token-to-access-the-api">Use the token to access the API</a>
</li>
<li><a href="#h-more-information">More information</a>
</li></ol></div>


<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-get-some-client-credentials"><span id="Get_some_client_credentials">Get some client credentials</span></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Client credentials are the username and password your application/website will use to access the ORCID API.  Anyone can register for read-only Public API credentials, ORCID members can register for the member API.</p>


<style>.ewd-ufaq-post-margin-symbol { color: #a6ce39 !important; }</style><div class="ewd-ufaq-faq-list ewd-ufaq-page-type-distinct ewd-ufaq-category-tabs-" id="ewd-ufaq-faq-list">

	<input type="hidden" name="show_on_load" value="" id="ewd-ufaq-show-on-load">
<input type="hidden" name="include_category" value="" id="ewd-ufaq-include-category">
<input type="hidden" name="exclude_category" value="" id="ewd-ufaq-exclude-category">
<input type="hidden" name="orderby" value="date" id="ewd-ufaq-orderby">
<input type="hidden" name="order" value="desc" id="ewd-ufaq-order">
<input type="hidden" name="post_count" value="-1" id="ewd-ufaq-post-count">
<input type="hidden" name="current_url" value="/documentation/api-tutorials/api-tutorial-read-data-on-a-record/" id="ewd-ufaq-current-url">
	
	
	<div class="ewd-ufaq-faqs">

		<div id="ewd-ufaq-faq-category-integration" class="ewd-ufaq-faq-category">
	
	<div class="ewd-ufaq-faq-category-title ">
		
		<h3 title="Click here to open Integration"><span id="Integration">
			Integration					</span></h3>

			
	</div>
	
	<div class="ewd-ufaq-faq-category-inner ">
<div class="ewd-ufaq-faq-div ewd-ufaq-faq-column-count-one ewd-ufaq-faq-responsive-columns- ewd-ufaq-faq-display-style-default ewd-ufaq-can-be-toggled" id="ewd-ufaq-post-20962-PDPUlPDVwN" data-post_id="20962">

		
	<div class="ewd-ufaq-faq-title ewd-ufaq-faq-toggle">
	
	<a class="ewd-ufaq-post-margin" href="#" role="button">

		<div class="ewd-ufaq-post-margin-symbol ewd-ufaq-square">
			<span>a</span>
		</div>

		<div class="ewd-ufaq-faq-title-text">

			<h4><span id="How_do_I_register_a_Public_API_client">
				How do I register a Public API client?			</span></h4>

		</div>

		<div class="ewd-ufaq-clear"></div>

	</a>
	
</div>
	
	<div class="ewd-ufaq-faq-body ewd-ufaq-hidden">

		
			
		
			<div class="ewd-ufaq-post-margin ewd-ufaq-faq-post">
	
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We recommend that developers test the Public API in the&nbsp;<a href="https://sandbox.orcid.org/signin" target="_blank" aria-label="undefined (opens in a new tab)" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow external" data-wpel-link="external">sandbox testing server</a>&nbsp;before using the production version.  Below are the steps on how to register for public API credentials in both the Sandbox and Production environments.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Sign into your ORCID record:<br>Production server:&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow external" href="https://orcid.org/signin" target="_blank" data-wpel-link="external">https://orcid.org/signin</a><br>Sandbox testing server:&nbsp;<a rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow external" href="https://sandbox.orcid.org/signin" target="_blank" data-wpel-link="external">https://sandbox.orcid.org/signin</a></li>



<li>Click on your name in the top right hand corner</li>



<li>Click&nbsp;<strong>Developer Tools&nbsp;</strong>from the menu option<br><strong>Note:</strong>&nbsp;In order to access Developer Tools, you must verify your email address. If you have not already verified your email address, you will be prompted to do before you can register for public API credentials</li>



<li>Read and agree to the ‘ORCID Public APIs Terms of Service</li>



<li>Click the “Register for ORCID Public API Credentials” button.</li>
</ul>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="884" src="https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/image-1-1024x884.png" alt="Screenshot of developer tools page" class="wp-image-30315" srcset="https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/image-1-1024x884.png 1024w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/image-1-300x259.png 300w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/image-1-768x663.png 768w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/image-1-1536x1326.png 1536w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/image-1-1320x1139.png 1320w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/image-1.png 1768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"></figure>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-completing-the-application-details-form"><span id="Completing_the_Application_Details_Form">Completing the Application Details Form</span></h4>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Once you have registered for your Public API Credentials you will be directed back to Developer Tools (<a href="https://orcid.org/developer-tools" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow external" data-wpel-link="external">https://orcid.org/developer-tools</a>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<a href="https://sandbox.orcid.org/developer-tools" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener nofollow external" data-wpel-link="external">https://sandbox.orcid.org/developer-tools</a>). </li>



<li>You need to complete the application details form presented to register a new application.
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Name</strong>: The name of your application. This will be displayed to users when they grant your application permission to get their ORCID iD, and it will be displayed in their&nbsp;<strong>Trusted organization list</strong>. We recommend using the name of your organization or service (e.g. a journal name).</li>



<li><strong>Application URL:</strong> The website the user can visit to learn more about your application. This will also be displayed in their&nbsp;<strong>Trusted organization list</strong>.</li>



<li><strong>Application Description</strong>: Information about the application that you are developing and how you will use the user’s ORCID iD. This will be displayed to users on the OAuth screen.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="alignright size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="484" src="https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Snip20230719_3-1024x484.png" alt="" class="wp-image-24501" srcset="https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Snip20230719_3-1024x484.png 1024w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Snip20230719_3-300x142.png 300w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Snip20230719_3-768x363.png 768w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Snip20230719_3-1536x726.png 1536w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Snip20230719_3-1320x624.png 1320w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Snip20230719_3.png 1980w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"></figure>
</div>


<h4 id="adding-redirect-uris" class="wp-block-heading"><span id="Adding_Redirect_URIs">Adding <strong>Redirect URIs</strong></span></h4>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Once the user has authorized your application, they will be returned to a URI that you specify. You must provide these URIs in advance or your integration users will experience an error.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Enter your redirect URI in the box provided</li>



<li>If you need to enter more than 1 redirect URI, click ‘Add another redirect URI’</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Please note:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Only&nbsp;<strong>HTTPS URIs</strong>&nbsp;are accepted in production</li>



<li>Domains registered&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;exactly match the domains used, including subdomains</li>



<li><strong>Register all redirect URIs fully where possible.</strong>&nbsp;This is the most secure option and what we recommend. For more information about redirect URIs, please see our&nbsp;<a href="https://info.orcid.org/ufaqs/how-do-redirect-uris-work/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" data-wpel-link="internal">redirect URI FAQ</a></li>
</ul>



<h4 id="saving-your-application" class="wp-block-heading"><span id="Saving_your_application">Saving your application</span></h4>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Once you have completed the application form and added your redirect URIs you can save your application. </p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Click ‘Save my application and generate my client ID and secret’</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You will be directed back to the developer tools page which will now include your Public API client credentials</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="276" src="https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/dev-tools-1024x276.png" alt="Image of client ID and client secret " class="wp-image-24505" srcset="https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/dev-tools-1024x276.png 1024w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/dev-tools-300x81.png 300w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/dev-tools-768x207.png 768w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/dev-tools-1536x415.png 1536w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/dev-tools-1320x356.png 1320w, https://info.orcid.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/dev-tools.png 2008w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"></figure>



<h4 id="updating-your-credentials" class="wp-block-heading"><span id="Updating_your_credentials">Updating your credentials</span></h4>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Making a change to your application information is very simple. </p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Edit the relevant information and then click ‘Save application’</li>
</ul>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-use-your-credentials"><span id="Use_your_credentials">Use your credentials</span></h4>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Now that you have your credentials, it’s time to start using the ORCID Public API! </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Please note that we can transfer your credentials to the member API if you become an <a href="https://info.orcid.org/about-membership/" data-wpel-link="internal">ORCID member</a> in the future. </p>
</div>
		
			
		
			
		
			
		
			
		
			
		
			<div class="ewd-ufaq-permalink">
	
	<a href="https://info.orcid.org/ufaqs/how-do-i-register-a-public-api-client/" data-wpel-link="internal">
		
		Permalink			
	</a>

</div>
		
			
		
			
		
	</div>

</div></div>

</div>

	</div>

	
</div>

<style>.ewd-ufaq-post-margin-symbol { color: #a6ce39 !important; }</style><div class="ewd-ufaq-faq-list ewd-ufaq-page-type-distinct ewd-ufaq-category-tabs-" id="ewd-ufaq-faq-list">

	<input type="hidden" name="show_on_load" value="" id="ewd-ufaq-show-on-load">
<input type="hidden" name="include_category" value="" id="ewd-ufaq-include-category">
<input type="hidden" name="exclude_category" value="" id="ewd-ufaq-exclude-category">
